# GreenScout — Git attributes
# Enforce LF line endings on shell scripts and tooling that runs in sh/bash,
# regardless of the contributor's core.autocrlf setting on Windows.

# Husky hooks are invoked by sh (see .husky/_/h shim) and must be LF.
.husky/* text eol=lf

# Generic shell scripts
*.sh text eol=lf

# Python files: enforce LF so `ruff format --check` (line-ending = "lf"
# in services/python/pyproject.toml) doesn't fail in lint-staged on Windows
# checkouts with core.autocrlf=true. The format tool itself outputs LF; the
# pre-commit gate sees the working-tree copy after lint-staged restores it.
*.py text eol=lf

# TypeScript / JavaScript files: enforce LF so `prettier --check`
# (endOfLine = "lf" in prettier.config.mjs) doesn't fail in lint-staged
# on Windows checkouts with core.autocrlf=true. The lint-staged stash /
# restore cycle would otherwise re-introduce CRLF after `prettier --write`
# already normalised the file to LF. Same rationale as the *.py rule above.
*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.jsx text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf
